      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Mediterranean cultures, the tendency toward overt demonstrations may indeed suggest these individuals are more prone to aggression or volatility in stressful settings. This expression of emotion can stem from a cultural norm that encourages individual expression and personal emotion as a valid form of communication. On the other hand, East Asians might become more stoic or avoidant as a way of handling stress. This stoicism is often a product of the cultural emphasis on maintaining social harmony over expressing personal emotions, even a negative ones like stress or anger. This could manifest as a reluctance to complain or openly acknowledge discomfort. Turning to avoidance, East Asians may subconsciously or consciously steer clear of conflict to maintain group cohesion or due to a perceived inability to manage intense emotional situations effectively.",
